1
00:00:07,225 --> 00:00:10,025
Last time, we found three animal groups.

2
00:00:10,315 --> 00:00:12,325
Amphibians, birds and fish.

3
00:00:12,585 --> 00:00:13,885
Three more to go!

4
00:00:14,018 --> 00:00:15,498
An ant and a spider.

5
00:00:15,648 --> 00:00:17,368
Which one is the insect?

6
00:00:19,874 --> 00:00:21,474
It's You against the Buddies.

7
00:00:21,744 --> 00:00:23,054
You lock in first.

8
00:00:23,324 --> 00:00:25,144
One finger for every point.

9
00:00:25,424 --> 00:00:28,114
A little grasshopper is hiding in this video.

10
00:00:28,364 --> 00:00:29,604
Can you spot it?

11
00:00:30,913 --> 00:00:31,793
Round one.

12
00:00:32,113 --> 00:00:33,733
Which one is an insect?

13
00:00:34,023 --> 00:00:35,123
One, the ant.

14
00:00:35,393 --> 00:00:36,483
Two, the spider.

15
00:00:36,803 --> 00:00:38,273
Show me with your fingers.

16
00:00:43,747 --> 00:00:44,727
Locked in!

17
00:00:44,855 --> 00:00:45,645
Two.

18
00:00:45,935 --> 00:00:47,805
It is tiny, and it crawls.

19
00:00:47,985 --> 00:00:49,155
Like a bug!

20
00:00:49,205 --> 00:00:49,835
One!

21
00:00:49,965 --> 00:00:50,845
The ant!

22
00:00:50,897 --> 00:00:51,617
One!

23
00:00:51,767 --> 00:00:53,017
But how do we know?

24
00:00:54,007 --> 00:00:55,247
Today you'll learn...

25
00:00:55,412 --> 00:00:56,862
How to spot an insect.

26
00:00:57,023 --> 00:00:58,523
How to spot a reptile.

27
00:00:58,684 --> 00:01:00,254
What cold-blooded means.

28
00:01:00,905 --> 00:01:01,845
Are you ready?

29
00:01:02,285 --> 00:01:03,055
Three!

30
00:01:03,435 --> 00:01:04,095
Two!

31
00:01:04,465 --> 00:01:05,115
One!

32
00:01:05,535 --> 00:01:06,255
Go!

33
00:01:07,544 --> 00:01:08,644
Count with me!

34
00:01:09,054 --> 00:01:11,234
One, two, three, four, five, six.

35
00:01:11,644 --> 00:01:12,704
Six legs!

36
00:01:12,842 --> 00:01:14,412
Two feelers on its head.

37
00:01:14,682 --> 00:01:16,272
And three body parts.

38
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:17,905
Now the spider.

39
00:01:18,255 --> 00:01:19,205
Eight legs!

40
00:01:19,475 --> 00:01:20,615
No feelers.

41
00:01:20,885 --> 00:01:22,125
Two body parts.

42
00:01:22,559 --> 00:01:24,119
The ant is the insect!

43
00:01:24,379 --> 00:01:25,809
The spider is not.

44
00:01:26,079 --> 00:01:27,819
It belongs to a different group.

45
00:01:28,629 --> 00:01:29,619
One finger?

46
00:01:29,939 --> 00:01:31,129
One finger up!

47
00:01:31,180 --> 00:01:31,830
Oops!

48
00:01:32,230 --> 00:01:33,490
Count the legs!

49
00:01:34,069 --> 00:01:35,369
Say it with me!

50
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:38,710
Insects have six legs and a pair of feelers.

51
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:43,110
The body of insects is divided into the head, thorax and abdomen.

52
00:01:50,639 --> 00:01:54,799
Insects have an outer covering that is usually hard and shell-like.

53
00:01:55,313 --> 00:01:58,143
Many adult insects have two pairs of wings.

54
00:01:58,423 --> 00:02:01,463
Some adult insects have only one pair of wings.

55
00:02:01,733 --> 00:02:03,493
Some do not have wings at all.

56
00:02:05,179 --> 00:02:05,879
My rule!

57
00:02:05,629 --> 00:02:08,009
If it has wings, it is an insect.

58
00:02:08,089 --> 00:02:09,009
A butterfly.

59
00:02:08,759 --> 00:02:10,079
A pigeon.

60
00:02:10,189 --> 00:02:11,399
Both insects!

61
00:02:11,671 --> 00:02:13,231
Something is not right.

62
00:02:13,501 --> 00:02:15,681
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

63
00:02:15,961 --> 00:02:16,921
Hold on!

64
00:02:22,434 --> 00:02:23,564
Arms crossed?

65
00:02:23,824 --> 00:02:24,994
One finger up!

66
00:02:25,284 --> 00:02:26,804
A pigeon has feathers.

67
00:02:27,074 --> 00:02:28,164
It is a bird.

68
00:02:28,444 --> 00:02:30,264
Count the legs, not the wings!

69
00:02:30,622 --> 00:02:31,352
Oops.

70
00:02:31,432 --> 00:02:32,972
Six legs, not wings!

71
00:02:34,255 --> 00:02:35,255
Round two.

72
00:02:35,555 --> 00:02:36,775
A monitor lizard!

73
00:02:37,085 --> 00:02:38,975
Its skin is dry and scaly.

74
00:02:39,255 --> 00:02:40,145
Which group?

75
00:02:40,485 --> 00:02:41,835
One, amphibians.

76
00:02:42,105 --> 00:02:43,445
Two, reptiles.

77
00:02:43,725 --> 00:02:44,845
Three, mammals.

78
00:02:45,125 --> 00:02:46,605
Show me with your fingers.

79
00:02:52,077 --> 00:02:53,057
Locked in!

80
00:02:53,185 --> 00:02:53,925
One!

81
00:02:54,035 --> 00:02:55,785
Four legs, like a frog.

82
00:02:55,838 --> 00:02:56,768
Two.

83
00:02:56,878 --> 00:02:58,998
Its skin is dry, not moist.

84
00:02:59,050 --> 00:02:59,670
Two!

85
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:01,130
Lizards like me!

86
00:03:01,409 --> 00:03:02,719
The answer is two.

87
00:03:02,999 --> 00:03:04,179
Reptiles!

88
00:03:07,047 --> 00:03:08,077
Two fingers?

89
00:03:08,347 --> 00:03:09,567
One finger up!

90
00:03:09,615 --> 00:03:10,535
I knew it!

91
00:03:10,605 --> 00:03:11,795
I'm a reptile!

92
00:03:12,223 --> 00:03:15,203
Most reptiles, except snakes, have four legs.

93
00:03:15,484 --> 00:03:18,274
Reptiles usually have dry and scaly skin.

94
00:03:18,554 --> 00:03:20,224
They breathe through their lungs.

95
00:03:20,514 --> 00:03:23,254
Most reptiles reproduce by laying eggs.

96
00:03:23,312 --> 00:03:24,632
I hatched from an egg!

97
00:03:24,981 --> 00:03:25,991
Be a scale!

98
00:03:26,281 --> 00:03:27,261
Shrink down.

99
00:03:27,531 --> 00:03:28,471
Quietly.

100
00:03:30,756 --> 00:03:33,476
You are one scale on a monitor lizard's back.

101
00:03:33,916 --> 00:03:35,586
You are dry, and tough.

102
00:03:36,092 --> 00:03:37,192
Early morning.

103
00:03:37,632 --> 00:03:39,762
The air is cool, so you are cool.

104
00:03:40,192 --> 00:03:41,662
The lizard is slow.

105
00:03:42,105 --> 00:03:43,775
Now it crawls into the sun.

106
00:03:44,215 --> 00:03:45,715
Sunlight lands on you.

107
00:03:46,135 --> 00:03:47,205
You warm up!

108
00:03:48,016 --> 00:03:49,716
At noon, it is too hot.

109
00:03:50,196 --> 00:03:51,056
Splash!

110
00:03:51,516 --> 00:03:52,856
Into the cool lake.

111
00:03:53,316 --> 00:03:54,496
You cool down.

112
00:03:59,094 --> 00:04:00,244
Say it with me!

113
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:02,990
Reptiles are cold-blooded animals.

114
00:04:03,030 --> 00:04:06,650
This means that they do not have a constant body temperature like

115
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:07,260
humans.

116
00:04:07,510 --> 00:04:11,460
Their body temperature changes with the environment that they are in.

117
00:04:16,411 --> 00:04:19,111
Cold-blooded does not mean I am always cold.

118
00:04:19,321 --> 00:04:20,701
I warm up in the sun!

119
00:04:21,204 --> 00:04:22,664
Show me your score hand!

120
00:04:22,954 --> 00:04:23,984
More than two?

121
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:25,634
You beat the Buddies.

122
00:04:25,934 --> 00:04:26,994
Three fingers?

123
00:04:27,274 --> 00:04:28,284
High five!

124
00:04:28,931 --> 00:04:30,621
Did you spot the grasshopper?

125
00:04:30,891 --> 00:04:32,441
It was on the lamp post!

126
00:04:32,711 --> 00:04:34,011
Is it an insect?

127
00:04:34,281 --> 00:04:35,581
Tell someone at home.

128
00:04:36,310 --> 00:04:38,510
Let's read today's key words together!

129
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:39,560
Ready?

130
00:04:39,897 --> 00:04:40,676
Insects.

131
00:04:42,151 --> 00:04:43,811
Head, thorax, abdomen.

132
00:04:45,847 --> 00:04:46,755
Reptiles.

133
00:04:48,403 --> 00:04:49,483
Cold-blooded.

134
00:04:51,023 --> 00:04:51,963
Well done!

135
00:04:53,060 --> 00:04:55,190
Next: this animal has wings.

136
00:04:55,460 --> 00:04:56,750
It flies at night.

137
00:04:57,030 --> 00:04:58,090
Is it a bird?

138
00:04:58,390 --> 00:04:59,970
Find out in Part Two!

139
00:05:01,635 --> 00:05:02,739
Say it with us!

140
00:05:03,539 --> 00:05:04,289
Ready?

141
00:05:04,412 --> 00:05:05,072
One!

142
00:05:05,412 --> 00:05:06,112
two!

143
00:05:06,417 --> 00:05:07,592
Now you know!
